    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d882">

                <pb facs="0832" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/–</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-11T19:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 13, 8.33
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2217. France formally through Helsingfors Consul recognized independence of
                    Finland. Reported France recognized Ukraine but unable verify. Know France sent
                    a general to Kiev but recognition probably confined thereto. Did France consult
                    us about Finnish recognition?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
